# Keep the build context small. Written before the first build on purpose:
# without it the context carries a 241 MB virtualenv, 54 MB of YARA rules and
# — worst — the entire malware corpus from ./samples, all of which is then
# discarded. Docker uploads the context to the daemon before doing anything.

.venv/
.git/
.github/

# The samples mount point. This is the important one: it is where the corpus
# is bind-mounted at runtime, and shipping malware into a build context is
# both slow and wrong.
samples/
reports/

# Fetched at runtime by `threatlens rules update`, into a named volume.
rules/yara/

# The PyInstaller binaries. The image installs flare-capa and flare-floss
# from the lockfile instead, so these 84.8 MB are dead weight here.
bin/capa
bin/floss

__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
build/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Author-facing documentation. The image does not need it.
docs/
UI_Report/

# Never ship a config that may hold a VirusTotal key. The image has its own
# config.docker.yaml and the key arrives through the environment.
config.yaml
